      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Illinois Central rail yards once covered most of the Loop, and the area now hosts the historic Michigan Boulevard District.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicago_Loop",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Former department store flagship sites, like the Marshall Field and Company Building, now house Macy’s on State Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicago_Loop",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Loop’s skyline is dominated by skyscrapers that have defined Chicago’s architectural identity since the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicago_Loop",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Despite covering just 1.58 square miles, the Loop packs attractions like the Art Institute of Chicago and historic theaters.",
